00:12:19.000 --> 00:13:02.000
reasons. And I think the same thing could be said of sort of gory horror movies or sort of more disgust-based horror movies. Some of the things I've been looking into with perspective, like, why do people enjoy the gory aspects? Or at least, why are those interesting to us, right? Why is that sometimes we find things interesting, but we don't necessarily enjoy them. And I think with with gore, what it can be is that at least when it comes to my morbid curiosity scale, it seems to be that it's more about learning sort of the limitations of the body and learning about the consequences of interacting with something dangerous. And so you can imagine that if you're watching a horror movie and the protagonist comes

