across a dead body, and the dead body has, you know, maybe a small cut on its neck, that doesn't give you a lot of information about the killer, right? It doesn't instill a lot of fear in you because anybody could cut another person's neck. It doesn't require a lot of strength or stealth or anything like that. But if their protagonist is walking along and they come across a body that's, you know, missing both of its arms and has its head smashed in, that then causes you to imagine something much more ferocious and terrifying and awful. And so, again, according to some of the studies that I've done and others have done, gruesome injuries seem to index formidability really well.

24
00:13:46.000 --> 00:14:19.000
