composure in the face of something that's uncertain, how to overcome things that seem scary. So if you're out playing and you're climbing a tree and it feels very scary. but your friends maybe are egging you on to keep going higher, or maybe you just want to go higher so you can see what's up there. These kinds of play teach kids how to manage their emotions, because if you go through your entire life, always avoiding any kind of a negative emotion, you're eventually going to have a negative emotion occur, right?

